        "original_id": "e1e8f62e-a3ca-5c14-ad34-4dbae914f013",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Matt Selman\n- Works: The Simpsons episodes, \"Behind the Laughter\", \"Natural Born Kissers\", \"Trilogy of Error\", \"Simpsons Bible Stories\", \"The Dad Who Knew Too Little\", \"The Food Wife\"\n- Organizations: Fox network, Annie Awards, Writers Guild of America Award\n\nFacts:\n- \"Behind the Laughter\" first aired on the Fox network in the United States on May 21, 2000.\n- Matt Selman wrote numerous episodes of The Simpsons, including \"Natural Born Kissers\", \"Behind the Laughter\", \"Trilogy of Error\", \"Simpsons Bible Stories\", \"The Dad Who Knew Too Little\", and \"The Food Wife\".\n- Matt Selman won an Annie Award for writing \"Simpsons Bible Stories\".\n- Matt Selman won a Writers Guild of America Award for writing \"The Dad Who Knew Too Little\".",
